<article class="ws-sheet">
<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; History by century</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The 8th century</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on the 700s: the states, events and people of the century. Use its page to find the answers.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/centuries/8th-century">Open the century page &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><p class="ws-how">Each number marks the capital or seat of a state that existed in 750 CE. Write its name from the word bank on the line with the same number.</p><figure class="ws-mapfig"><svg class="map map-world ws-map" viewBox="0 0 10903 5739" role="img" aria-label="Map: 8 numbered states of the world in 750 CE"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><g class="ws-pins"><g><circle cx="7771" cy="1192" r="185"/><text x="7771" y="1270" font-size="222">1</text></g><g><circle cx="5054" cy="728" r="185"/><text x="5054" y="806" font-size="222">2</text></g><g><circle cx="5709" cy="970" r="185"/><text x="5709" y="1048" font-size="222">3</text></g><g><circle cx="8260" cy="1139" r="185"/><text x="8260" y="1217" font-size="222">4</text></g><g><circle cx="7833" cy="2434" r="185"/><text x="7833" y="2511" font-size="222">5</text></g><g><circle cx="4782" cy="1851" r="185"/><text x="4782" y="1929" font-size="222">6</text></g><g><circle cx="7188" cy="1956" r="185"/><text x="7188" y="2033" font-size="222">7</text></g><g><circle cx="6134" cy="1224" r="185"/><text x="6134" y="1302" font-size="222">8</text></g></g></svg><figcaption>The world in 750 CE</figcaption></figure><p class="ws-bank"><b>Word bank:</b> Srivijaya Empire &middot; Silla &middot; Ghana Empire &middot; Kingdom of the Franks &middot; Pallava dynasty &middot; Umayyad Caliphate &middot; Byzantine Empire &middot; Tang Dynasty</p><ol class="ws-blanks"><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li></ol></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the events from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Byzantine Iconoclasm</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Berber Revolt</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Abbasid Revolution</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>An Lushan Rebellion</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Roncevaux Pass</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Saxon Wars</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right dates next to each person. Look them up in the encyclopedia.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Bede</li><li>Pepin of Italy</li><li>Saint Boniface</li><li>Beatus of Liébana</li><li>Hisham I of Córdoba</li><li>Paul the Deacon</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>757–796</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 720–c. 799</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>777–810</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 673–735</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 675–754</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 730–c. 800</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>In the 700s, 101 recorded states were founded and 66 came to an end. Choose one of each from the century page. What happened to them?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The great powers of the age included the Tang Dynasty, the Kingdom of the Franks and the Byzantine Empire. Choose one: what made it strong in these hundred years, and what threatened it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one event from the list and one person. How might they be connected? Use the encyclopedia to find out.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>If you could visit one place in the 8th century, where would you go, and what would you hope to see?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/centuries/8th-century. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The 8th century</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Tang Dynasty <span>618 CE – 907 CE</span></li><li>Kingdom of the Franks <span>481 CE – 843 CE</span></li><li>Byzantine Empire <span>330 CE – 1453 CE</span></li><li>Silla <span>57 BCE – 935 CE</span></li><li>Srivijaya Empire <span>650 CE – 1377 CE</span></li><li>Ghana Empire <span>300 CE – 1240 CE</span></li><li>Pallava dynasty <span>275 CE – 897 CE</span></li><li>Umayyad Caliphate <span>661 CE – 750 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Byzantine Iconoclasm <span>730–787 CE; 815–843 CE</span></li><li>Berber Revolt <span>739–743 CE</span></li><li>Abbasid Revolution <span>750</span></li><li>An Lushan Rebellion <span>755–763</span></li><li>Saxon Wars <span>772–804</span></li><li>Battle of Roncevaux Pass <span>778</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Bede <span>4: c. 673–735</span></li><li>Pepin of Italy <span>3: 777–810</span></li><li>Saint Boniface <span>5: c. 675–754</span></li><li>Beatus of Liébana <span>6: c. 730–c. 800</span></li><li>Hisham I of Córdoba <span>1: 757–796</span></li><li>Paul the Deacon <span>2: c. 720–c. 799</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers name states, people and events from the century page.</p></section></div></details>
